  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "HEMATOMA\nwhen there is a fracture, the blood vessel cuts and this leads
    to blood outflow, in the blood are series of cellular activities and this leads
    to the\_ clumping together of cells, forming a thick red swelling around the
    fracture known as Hematoma, this process is completed within 1st week of the
    fracture, among the cells that assembled at the fractured point are the RBC,
    platelet, WBC, MSC`s and others.\nThe mesenchymal cell (MSC`S), which is our
    focus here produces the chondrocytes, Osteoblast and the Osteoclast, which are
    the key tools to the beginning and healing of the bone fracture."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
